5ESS-EMU
========

5ESS-EMU is a small Perl simulator inspired by the AT&T/Lucent 5ESS craft
environment, with a Pacific Bell-flavoured default office.  It is intended as
an educational and historical toy: a craft-shell style program with simulated
recent-change/verify work, alarms, SCC jobs, ROP output and switch state.

It is not a real switch administration tool.  It does not administer real
telecommunications equipment and is not affiliated with AT&T, Lucent, Nokia,
Pacific Bell or any successor entity.

Current state
-------------

The tree currently contains a terminal craft shell in `5ESS.pl`, supporting
modules under `lib/`, sample configuration under `etc/`, and historical
reference material under `raw docs/`.

The immediate development goal is to stabilise the existing terminal simulator
before adding a CGI craft-console interface.

Running
-------

Check syntax first:

    perl -c 5ESS.pl
    perl -Ilib -c lib/*.pm

Run the terminal simulator:

    perl 5ESS.pl

By default state is written under `./var`.  To keep separate state trees, set
`5ESS_STATE_DIR`:

    5ESS_STATE_DIR=/tmp/5ess-demo perl 5ESS.pl

Tests
-----

Run the test suite with:

    prove -Ilib t

or, after generating a Makefile:

    perl Makefile.PL
    make test

The tests use temporary state directories and should not touch a developer's
local `var/` tree.

Source material
---------------

Original project source code is BSD 2-Clause licensed.  Historical manuals and
other third-party reference materials are used only as research sources.  They
are not covered by the project's BSD licence unless expressly stated by their
respective rights holders.

Style
-----

The intended style is a late-1990s or early-2000s Perl/Unix open-source
project: plain files, plain Perl, terse operator output, fixed-width terminal
screens and practical documentation.  New code should preserve that feel.
